  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Health 2 Project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Project Development Objective is to improve the quality and overall cost-effectiveness of health care services in Uzbekistan. This will be achieved through:  (a)   completion of the primary care program in 8 regions  (Samarkand, Sukhandarya, Namangan, Andijon, Djizzak, Ferghana, Navoiy, and Syr Darya) and other regions as agreed, and institutionalization of general practitioners nationally;  (b)  extending financing and management reforms related to efficiency and effectiveness of service delivery;  (c) improving public health services, including surveillance, training in public health and control of communicable disease; and  (d) building capacity in the Ministry of Health to better monitor and evaluate the reforms, and better manage the restructuring process.</narrative>
  </description>
